      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-29 (WS-E/F/G complete + the daemon seam WIRED).\n\nE-2/E-4. A step now DECLARES where and how it runs (StepDeclaration: requiredCapabilities, target,\nattended, credentialRefs, offlinePolicy) and the router places it on that, not on \"newest live\nsocket for this owner\" — which meant a step written for the machine with the card reader ran on\nwhatever laptop connected last. Defaults are the CLOSED ones: declaring nothing asks for nothing\nand STOPS (offlinePolicy 'fail'). `cloud` is not a machine; `pinned` is that machine or nothing, no\nsubstitute; `any:<cap>` selects only from machines the ORG GRANTED (I-3). No match returns\nundefined so the CALLER applies the offline policy — placement reports a fact about the fleet, the\nresponse belongs to the run.\n\nF-3/F-4/F-5. Login recipes are FIXED DATA in api/assets/login-recipes/, loaded through a validator\nthat refuses script-shaped selectors, refuses unrecognised fields rather than ignoring them, and is\nall-or-nothing. A recipe says WHERE the fields are; it never says what to do — the typist is the\nonly primitive handling a decrypted credential against a live page, so anything steering it is\ninside the credential's trust boundary. `signature` split from `login` (I8): signing is legal\nauthorship bound to the card in the reader, so it routes ATTENDED while a login RELAYS. And a\nCREDENTIAL-ADJACENT failure never reaches the rehearsal fixer — handing an unfamiliar login form to\nan LLM means its output picks which field receives the password.\n\nG-4/G-5. Checkout asks health FIRST, then egress. An expired/unhealthy session returns a\nRE-ESTABLISHMENT ROUTE chosen by provenance (card ceremony -> attended, password -> typist, unknown\n-> attended, the conservative direction). A residential-bound session refuses checkout when only\ndatacenter egress is available: same cookie, different continent is the pattern fraud systems flag,\nand another machine's residential line is not a substitute.\n\nTHE SEAM IS WIRED. setDaemonConnectionResolver at server.ts now returns a live connection, so\nlocal_command and daemon browser steps are reachable end to end. The plan calls this \"the single\nmost dangerous ordering mistake available\" and gates it behind H-1, H-4, J-4, J-7 — all in. The\nproperty that makes it safe: wiring grants NOTHING. invokeTool refuses before sending unless the ORG\ngranted that capability on that machine, re-read PER INVOCATION so a mid-run revoke stops the next\nstep. tool.invoke/tool.result gained the awaiting coordinator they lacked; every invocation settles\n(refused / unreachable / timeout / disconnect), so a run never hangs on a machine."
    },
